    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "No continuous metric for real client-received push latency",
      "gridPos": { "h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 19 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "`marketplace_subscription_push_duration_seconds` measures only the in-process `pubSub.publish()` call - not the full NATS/WebSocket round-trip to a real subscribed client. That fuller measurement is validated periodically via `scripts/load-test.ts` (Phase 8) instead - see `docs/module-07-phase-8-load-test-results.md` for the last real measurement (p99 127.5ms at 25-round scale, well under the 500ms target). Same scope boundary Module 05's own dashboard documents for its analogous push metric (ADR-0071/0072)."
      }
    },
